  "note": "Election of the Holywood Urban Council, polled Wednesday 21 May 1952 (Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5). Fourteen candidates for nine seats; the result names only the nine elected; the five defeated, F. F. Graham, Mrs. M. E. Blampied, J. S. Middleton, W. E. Russell and Harold F. Winter, are named in the nominations (Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1952, p. 6) and entered without votes, which no paper read prints. Vote figures verified against the article image. Losers not printed: the result (Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5, re-checked 13 Nov 2026) names only the nine elected of the 14 candidates.",
  "losersNotPrinted": true,
  "correctionNote": "Corrected from the page image of Belfast News-Letter, 22 May 1952, p. 5 (council-audit, Nov 2026): Dr. H. L. Donnan's vote 1,667 -> 1,567 as printed (the digit matches the paper's 5s, not its 6s). Completed from the page image of the Belfast News-Letter, 8 May 1952, p. 6 (w19-council-fix-east, Nov 2026): the fourteen nominations name the five candidates not elected (F. F. Graham, Mrs. M. E. Blampied, J. S. Middleton, W. E. Russell, Harold F. Winter), now entered without votes; no withdrawals (the result counts 14 candidates)."
